# Test-only mod for W1-P2 (WAVE1-RUNBOOK.md SS2.W1 / WV-D28 / WV-D42).
#
# operationNamesFirst/Last feed BriefingState's "random operation names" block
# (BriefingState.cpp:171-187) and CoopHandshake::mintMissionLabels()'s exact
# replica of it. They are RAW strings, concatenated, never tr()'d - the vanilla
# UI wraps the result in STR_OPERATION_UC ("OPERATION> {0}").
#
# 24 x 24 = 576 combinations: if the SS2.W1 re-mint suppression regressed, the
# host's BriefingState would re-roll and land on a different name than the one
# the offer already shipped to the client with p = 575/576. (The deterministic
# half of that regression is the "operation-name re-mint SUPPRESSED" log line
# test_rw_mission_labels.py also asserts; this pool is what makes the VALUE
# comparison meaningful rather than vacuous.)
operationNamesFirst:
  - Amber
  - Blazing
  - Crimson
  - Dauntless
  - Emerald
  - Frozen
  - Gilded
  - Howling
  - Iron
  - Jagged
  - Keen
  - Lucid
  - Midnight
  - Northern
  - Onyx
  - Prowling
  - Quiet
  - Rolling
  - Silent
  - Thunder
  - Umber
  - Violet
  - Whisper
  - Zephyr
operationNamesLast:
  - Anvil
  - Bastion
  - Cascade
  - Dagger
  - Ember
  - Falcon
  - Gambit
  - Harrier
  - Ibis
  - Javelin
  - Kestrel
  - Lantern
  - Mantis
  - Nomad
  - Osprey
  - Pinnacle
  - Quarry
  - Rampart
  - Sentinel
  - Talon
  - Uplink
  - Vanguard
  - Warden
  - Yeoman
